ue, error rate 0.002. Follow-ups: investigate root cause of v2.3.1 failures, investigate the orchestrator partial failure during the first rollback, and decide when v2.3.1 can be retried.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 was the most recent production release that was healthy. v2.3.1 is unhealthy in production, and v2.3.1-rc was only deployed to staging.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the regions mixed (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). I retried the same rollback once, and it completed.\n- **Current state:** All regions are on v2.3.0, healthy, with an error rate of 0.002 (down from 0.18).\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback, the partial failure and retry, and the follow-ups. Those are the root cause of v2.3.1, the orchestrator error, and when v2.3.1 can be retried.", "type": "text"}]}]}